LiteLLM gateway runs vLLM, which requires "encoding_format": "float" on /v1/embeddings. itsm-app was only sending {"model": "...", "input": "..."}, which returns 400 Bad Request.

Temporal Workaround

Without encoding_format → 400
With "encoding_format": "float" and model Nomic-embed-text-v2-moe → 200 OK
What I did on your cluster
Rebuilt itsm-app with a one-line patch to kb_embeddings.py
Rolled out the new image — rag_search_kb now returns no_indexed_articles instead of embedding_failed (embeddings work; KB just needs re-indexing)
What I added to the repo
Install now automatically patches itsm-app during image build and before RAG setup:

roles/demo_platform/tasks/build_itsm_app_image.yml — clone + patch + binary build
roles/demo_platform/tasks/ensure_itsm_app_vllm_embedding_patch.yml — rebuild if the running pod lacks the patch
Wired into install_itsm_app.yml and configure_itsm_app_rag.yml

-------------------
The Nomic-embed-text-v2-moe model on your LiteLLM/vLLM gateway rejects inputs longer than ~1500 characters with 400 Bad Request.
Truncate index text to 1500 chars in the itsm-app build patch (alongside the existing encoding_format: float patch)